# Spherical edge extensions: accepted evidence and observation prototype

The [synthesis paper](../../papers/SPHERICAL_EDGE_EXTENSIONS/README.md) explains the completed BOUNDARY-10/11/12 static construction.

- [Accepted reports and inventories](accepted/) retain their original bytes and source namespaces.
- [BOUNDARY-11 internal review](reviews/boundary11/BOUNDARY11_GPT_SCIENTIFIC_REVIEW.md) and [BOUNDARY-12 internal review](reviews/boundary12/BOUNDARY12_GPT_SCIENTIFIC_REVIEW.md) are complete separate review trees. These are internal GPT reviews, not external peer review.
- [Unchanged HTML observation prototype](viewer/BOUNDARY12_VIEWER.html): download and open locally in a WebGL-capable browser. GitHub's file page is not an interactive hosting service. Read [known limitations, including V01](viewer/KNOWN_LIMITATIONS.md) first.
- [Future questions](future/OPEN_QUESTIONS.md) and [unchanged observer proposal](future/APP_OBSERVER_DESIGN.md) are separately labelled deferred work, not implementation.

The extended spatial graph, convex enclosure, observer sphere and any proposed physical wall are different objects. No kernel or application integration is present. Accepted mathematics is completed; a known prototype issue does not turn its exact results into open questions.

`SOURCE_DISPOSITION.csv` maps original submission members and all candidate files to their dispositions. See the paper's [access guide](../../papers/SPHERICAL_EDGE_EXTENSIONS/publication/v0.1/ACCESS_AND_EVIDENCE_MAP.md) for exact-path prerequisites and curated omissions. Inert original scripts have **not** been rewritten to run in this relocated layout. Their original execution counts are historical records, not newly run authoring tests.

No new licence is granted. Repository Apache-2.0 software scope does not automatically cover these scientific materials. Embedded/bundled Plotly notices are preserved. Disclosure and rights questions in the review package must be resolved before later publication authorization.
